<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="integrity">
  <title>Preserving the Course's Integrity</title>

  <p>By taking this course, students agree to preserve the integrity of the course:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>
        You may <alert>not</alert> use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to
        complete your assignments and assessments in this course.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        All assignments in this course are individual assignments. Having said
        so, I would like to encourage you to discuss the course concepts with
        your classmates and with me. When it is time to take an assessment, I
        expect you to do the work independently. This is the only way that I
        will be able to tell what you have learned.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Please do not post any of the course material on the internet. If this
        basic expectation is not followed, it will violate copyright laws, and
        it will spoil the learning experience of future students of the course.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Violation of academic integrity may result in receiving an F in the
        course and being reported to the Office of Student Life.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
